endobj
193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The BRSR Core standards provide a robust framework for environmental, social, and governance \(ESG\) disclosures. The structure is divided into two parts. Part A focuses on general requirements, such as intensity-based calculations for greenhouse gas \(GHG\) emissions, water consumption, energy usage, and waste management. Metrics are calculated using revenue adjusted for purchasing power parity \(PPP\) and output-based intensity. Part B addresses attribute-specific requirements, including detailed metrics for GHG emissions, water and energy footprints, circular waste management, employee wellbeing, gender diversity, and inclusive development.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Provisional Carbon Accounting Proxy Methodology)
/E (Provisional Carbon Accounting Proxy Methodology)
/Alt ()
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
195 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Recognizing data challenges faced by enterprises, SEBI has introduced a provisional Carbon Accounting Proxy \(CAP\) methodology for estimating Scope 1 and Scope 2 emissions. This spend-based approach leverages financial data to estimate emissions in cases where direct measurement data is unavailable. The CAP methodology involves converting financial expenditure on fuels and electricity into quantity-based estimates, which are then used to calculate emissions using recognized emission factors. While useful for early compliance, this approach is intended for short-term use, with enterprises encouraged to transition to quantity-based methods for greater accuracy.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
196 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Key Metrics and Disclosure Requirements)
/E (Key Metrics and Disclosure Requirements)
/Alt ()
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
197 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The standards mandate the reporting of critical sustainability metrics. These include GHG emissions, water and energy consumption, and waste intensity calculated against revenue or production outputs. For employee wellbeing, entities must disclose expenditures on health and safety measures, maternity/paternity benefits, and mental health programs. Gender diversity metrics include the proportion of wages paid to female employees and complaints filed under the Prevention of Sexual Harassment \(POSH\) Act. Companies are also required to report on customer and supplier engagement practices, including data breach incidents and openness in business transactions.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
198 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Governance and Sustainability Goals)
/E (Governance and Sustainability Goals)
/Alt ()
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
199 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The BRSR Core standards are designed to align listed entities with global ESG practices, fostering accountability and sustainable business operations. By standardizing disclosures and introducing practical methodologies like CAP, SEBI seeks to address implementation challenges while ensuring progress toward long-term sustainability goals. These efforts underscore the commitment to making Indian enterprises globally competitive and environmentally responsible.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
