203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The Environmental, Social, and Governance \(ESG\) landscape in India is undergoing a significant transformation, driven by regulatory advancements and a growing emphasis on sustainable business practices. The Securities and Exchange Board of India \(SEBI\) has introduced the Business Responsibility and Sustainability Report \(BRSR\) framework, mandating the top 1,000 listed companies by market capitalization to disclose their ESG activities in a standardized format. The BRSR, divided into General Disclosures, Management Disclosures, and Principle-wise Performance, aligns with the National Guidelines on Responsible Business Conduct \(NGRBC\) and enhances transparency and stakeholder assessment of non-financial performance. To further streamline reporting, SEBI launched 'BRSR Core' in July 2023, featuring key performance indicators tailored to India's context, such as job creation in small towns and wages paid to women. Additionally, SEBI has expanded the sustainable finance framework, proposing green securitization and broadening the scope of instruments like social bonds, sustainable bonds, and sustainability-linked bonds. These initiatives reflect SEBI's commitment to embedding ESG factors into financial decision-making and promoting responsible business conduct. With increasing regulatory requirements and SEBI's proactive approach, companies in India are being encouraged to integrate ESG considerations into their strategies, fostering environmental sustainability, social well-being, and strong governance. These efforts aim to provide stakeholders with comprehensive insights into ESG performance, enabling informed decision-making and long-term value creation in the corporate sector.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
204 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Objectives of the survey)
/E (Objectives of the survey)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
205 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The objective of the survey report is to gather insights into the current state of ESG integration within organizations, focusing on key aspects such as the development of an ESG roadmap and materiality assessment, the challenges and best practices in preparing ESG reports under frameworks like Business Responsibility and Sustainability Reporting \(BRSR\), and the evolving requirements of BRSR Core. The survey also aims to explore the role and impact of assurance in enhancing the credibility of ESG reports and aligning them with stakeholder expectations. Furthermore, it seeks to understand how organizations are building a compelling business case for ESG and long term sustainability, particularly in terms of engaging and securing board-level commitment to ESG strategies. This comprehensive analysis will help identify trends, gaps, and opportunities to drive meaningful progress in ESG implementation and reporting practices.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
