216 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Regulatory compliance, building customer trust, and presenting clear business strategies are key drivers for ESG disclosures. Additionally, risk management plays a significant role, while investor demands and competitive pressure are less influential. Our respondents believed that regulatory compliance is the most significant driver for organizations to make ESG disclosures, closely followed by the need to build long-term customer trust and clearly present business strategies. Strengthening risk management also plays an important role, while factors such as responding to investor requests and competitive pressure are less influential in driving ESG disclosure efforts.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
217 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 109 0 R
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
218 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The analysis reveals that regulatory compliance is the strongest motivator \(100%\) for organizations to make ESG disclosures, followed by building long-term customer reputation \(87%\) and presenting business strategy more clearly \(67%\). Factors like risk management \(58%\) also hold significant influence, while responding to investor requests \(22%\) and competitive pressure \(0%\) are less critical drivers. This suggests that while some companies may be hesitant to voluntarily disclose ESG data, regulatory mandates can serve as a powerful catalyst for increased transparency. This highlights the importance of clear guidelines and consistent enforcement to encourage broader adoption of ESG reporting practices.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
