/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The analysis indicates that 80% of organizations face challenges in implementing a robust ESG data management system due to a combination of factors. A lack of internal expertise is a challenge for 20% of organizations, while issues like high implementation costs, integration with existing infrastructure, and inconsistent data from multiple sources do not appear to be significant concerns \(0%\). To bridge the gap in internal expertise, organizations should prioritize investing in training and development programs to equip their employees with the necessary knowledge and skills. Furthermore, leveraging technology can significantly streamline data collection, analysis, and reporting processes, making ESG reporting more efficient and effective.)
